{
  "configuration_id": "config_045",
  "reason": "Evidence: The largest single gain observed is from multiprofile+avgpool aggregation in the RNA-only setting (config_028: 0.650 vs config_009 singleprofile: 0.520, a +0.13 jump). Separately, adding image to singleprofile RNA gave a modest boost (config_039: 0.537 vs config_009: 0.520). Uncertainty: We do not yet know whether the multiprofile+avgpool gain transfers to the multimodal setting or whether the two effects are additive/synergistic. This experiment (multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, weighted) directly tests that combination while keeping all other choices at their best-evidenced values (scvi_n200 as top RNA encoder, imagenet_vit_l as the image encoder used in the only other multimodal result, avgpool as the aggregation that drove the largest gain, weighted fusion as in config_039). It is a clean one-variable extension of config_028 (adding image+fusion) and of config_039 (adding multiprofile+avgpool), making it the most informative next step under budget constraints."
}

